<title>RUSSIA: New 105-day Russia T-bill tranche yields 40.35 pct.</title>
<headline>New 105-day Russia T-bill tranche yields 40.35 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average annualised yield on a new 105-day tranche of GKO discount Treasury bills was 40.35 percent at an auction on Wednesday, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:  </p>
<p>				     Nov 19		  Nov 13</p>
<p>    Series number		22044		   22038</p>
<p>    Issue volume		 3.00 trln rbls	3.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		1.00 million		1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)	     4.88 trln	     4.73 trln</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)	     2.98 trln	     2.16 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds		     2.67 trln	     2.04 trln</p>
<p>    Average price	     89.60 pct	     94.49 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price   89.52 pct	     94.40 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield	     40.35 pct	     38.01 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accpeted yield  40.70 pct	     38.67 pct</p>
<p>    Issue date		  Nov 20, 1996	  Nov 13, 1996</p>
<p>    Original issue date     August 7, 1996	June 26, 1997</p>
<p>    Tenor (remaining)	 105 days		56 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date	     March 5, 1997	 Jan 8, 1997</p>
<p>The issue closed at 40.48 percent on Tuesday. The paper yielded an average 106.12 percent when it was first issued.</p>
<p>On November 20 the finance ministry will also auction eight trillion roubles of new six-month T-bills (series 22059).</p>
<p>It will also repay about 6.33 trillion roubles in maturing three-month bills (series 21068).</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
